      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "After headache, low back pain is the most common cause of intractable pain. It is a condition experienced by 50-80% of the world's population, ranking first among all health problems in frequency of occurrence. This chapter focuses on the treatment of chronic low back pain and describes the pain program at the University of Miami Comprehensive Pain and Rehabilitation Center."},
